er, consider that any additional solutions \\((x, y)\\) must also make \\(x^2\\) and \\(y^2\\) sum to an exact square number.\n\n5. **Check for All Numbers Being Sums of Squares:**\n   We assess whether there exist integers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) such that\n   \\[\n   x^2 + y^2 = 199^2\n   \\]\n   Note that for \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) to be integers and non-zero, the sum of their squares \\(x^2 + y^2\\) must also equal the square of 199, and importantly, modulo 4 the sums of squares  \\(0\\) or \\(1\\) are achievable but not \\(3\\):\n\n   \\[\n   199 \\equiv 3 \\text{ (mod 4)}, \\quad 199^2 = 39601 \\equiv 1 \\text{ (mod 4)}\n   \\]\n\n   However, to evaluate if \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) can achieve:\n   \\[\n   4k^2 + (2l-1)^2 \\neq 1 \\text{ (mod 4 projections imply contradictions)}\n   \\]\n   \n   This reassures us no further non-trivial integer solutions exists other than trivial ones already mentioned.\n\n6. **Conclusion:**\n   Since the only integer solutions to \\(x^2 + y^2 = 39601\\) that lie on the circle are along its four main axes, the total number of lattice points is:\n   \\[\n   (199, 0), (0, 199), (-199, 0), (0, -199)\n   \\]\n   Thus, the number of lattice points on the circumference of the circle is:\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{4}\n   \\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "The company \"Superheroes, Inc.\" urgently called Superman and Flash to perform some work on building protective structures against a hurricane. It is known that Flash's productivity is twice that of Superman's productivity. Each superhero's payment depends only on the time they spend on the job and is given by the formula \\( w = \\frac{90}{t} \\), where \\( w \\) is the amount of money the superhero receives, and \\( t \\) is the time in minutes they spend on the job. Flash was 1 minute late to start the construction, and during this time, Superman managed to complete \\( 10\\% \\) of the total work. Both superheroes completed the 