1a3\n\nDivide both sides by \u221a3:\n\n(\u03bb - 1)/(1 - 3\u03bb) = \u03bb\n\nMultiply both sides by (1 - 3\u03bb):\n\n\u03bb - 1 = \u03bb(1 - 3\u03bb)\n\nExpand RHS:\n\n\u03bb - 1 = \u03bb - 3\u03bb\u00b2\n\nSubtract \u03bb from both sides:\n\n-1 = -3\u03bb\u00b2\n\nMultiply both sides by -1:\n\n1 = 3\u03bb\u00b2 \u2192 \u03bb\u00b2 = 1/3 \u2192 \u03bb = \u00b11/\u221a3\n\nBut since \u03bb is a ratio of lengths, it must be between 0 and 1. Hence, \u03bb = 1/\u221a3 \u2248 0.577.\n\nBut let's rationalize the denominator: 1/\u221a3 = \u221a3/3 \u2248 0.577. So \u03bb = \u221a3 / 3.\n\nBut let me check my calculations again.\n\nStarting with slope BM:\n\nCoordinates of M: (1 - 1.5\u03bb, (\u221a3/2)\u03bb)\n\nCoordinates of B: (0.5, \u221a3/2)\n\nDifference in x: (1 - 1.5\u03bb) - 0.5 = 0.5 - 1.5\u03bb\n\nDifference in y: (\u221a3/2 \u03bb) - (\u221a3/2) = \u221a3/2 (\u03bb - 1)\n\nSlope BM: [\u221a3/2 (\u03bb - 1)] / [0.5 - 1.5\u03bb] = [\u221a3 (\u03bb - 1)] / [1 - 3\u03bb]\n\nSlope BN:\n\nCoordinates of N: (-0.5, \u221a3/2 - \u03bb\u221a3)\n\nCoordinates of B: (0.5, \u221a3/2)\n\nDifference in x: -0.5 - 0.5 = -1\n\nDifference in y: (\u221a3/2 - \u03bb\u221a3) - \u221a3/2 = -\u03bb\u221a3\n\nSlope BN: (-\u03bb\u221a3) / (-1) = \u03bb\u221a3\n\nSetting slopes equal:\n\n[\u221a3 (\u03bb - 1)] / [1 - 3\u03bb] = \u03bb\u221a3\n\nDivide both sides by \u221a3:\n\n(\u03bb - 1)/(1 - 3\u03bb) = \u03bb\n\nMultiply both sides by (1 - 3\u03bb):\n\n\u03bb - 1 = \u03bb(1 - 3\u03bb)\n\nExpand RHS:\n\n\u03bb - 1 = \u03bb - 3\u03bb\u00b2\n\nSubtract \u03bb:\n\n-1 = -3\u03bb\u00b2 \u2192 3\u03bb\u00b2 = 1 \u2192 \u03bb\u00b2 = 1/3 \u2192 \u03bb = 1/\u221a3 = \u221a3/3 \u2248 0.577\n\nWhich is valid since \u03bb must be between 0 and 1.\n\nTherefore, \u03bb = \u221a3 / 3.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe value of \\(\\lambda\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}}\\).", "deepseek_solution": "To solve the given geometry problems, we proceed as follows:\n\n### Problem 1: Proving Triangles \\( 