N = sin20\u00b0, so triangle BMN is isoceles with BM = BN.\n\n3. MN: distance from M to N.\n\nCoordinates of M: (cos20\u00b0, 0)\n\nCoordinates of N: ( sin\u00b220\u00b0 + cos20\u00b0, sin20\u00b0(1 - cos20\u00b0 ) )\n\nDifference in x-coordinates: ( sin\u00b220\u00b0 + cos20\u00b0 ) - cos20\u00b0 = sin\u00b220\u00b0\n\nDifference in y-coordinates: sin20\u00b0(1 - cos20\u00b0 ) - 0 = sin20\u00b0(1 - cos20\u00b0 )\n\nTherefore, MN = sqrt( (sin\u00b220\u00b0)^2 + ( sin20\u00b0(1 - cos20\u00b0 ) )^2 )\n\nLet's compute:\n\n= sqrt( sin\u207420\u00b0 + sin\u00b220\u00b0(1 - cos20\u00b0)^2 )\n\nFactor out sin\u00b220\u00b0:\n\n= sin20\u00b0 sqrt( sin\u00b220\u00b0 + (1 - cos20\u00b0)^2 )\n\nLet's compute the expression under the square root:\n\nsin\u00b220\u00b0 + (1 - cos20\u00b0)^2\n\nExpand (1 - cos20\u00b0)^2: 1 - 2cos20\u00b0 + cos\u00b220\u00b0\n\nSo total expression:\n\nsin\u00b220\u00b0 + 1 - 2cos20\u00b0 + cos\u00b220\u00b0 = (sin\u00b220\u00b0 + cos\u00b220\u00b0) + 1 - 2cos20\u00b0 = 1 + 1 - 2cos20\u00b0 = 2(1 - cos20\u00b0)\n\nTherefore, MN = sin20\u00b0 sqrt( 2(1 - cos20\u00b0) )\n\nBut 1 - cos20\u00b0 = 2sin\u00b210\u00b0, using the identity 1 - cos\u03b8 = 2sin\u00b2(\u03b8/2). So:\n\nMN = sin20\u00b0 sqrt( 2 * 2sin\u00b210\u00b0 ) = sin20\u00b0 sqrt(4 sin\u00b210\u00b0 ) = sin20\u00b0 * 2 sin10\u00b0 = 2 sin10\u00b0 sin20\u00b0\n\nAlternatively, using exact expressions.\n\nSo, MN = 2 sin10\u00b0 sin20\u00b0\n\nWait, let's confirm the identity step:\n\n1 - cos20\u00b0 = 2 sin\u00b210\u00b0, yes, since \u03b8 = 20\u00b0, so \u03b8/2 = 10\u00b0, so 1 - cos20\u00b0 = 2 sin\u00b210\u00b0. Therefore:\n\nsqrt(2(1 - cos20\u00b0)) = sqrt(2 * 2 sin\u00b210\u00b0 ) = sqrt(4 sin\u00b210\u00b0 ) = 2 sin10\u00b0. Therefore, MN = sin20\u00b0 * 2 sin10\u00b0, which is 2 sin10\u00b0 sin20\u00b0, correct.\n\nTherefore, MN = 2 sin10\u00b0 sin20\u00b0\n\nNow, we have all sides:\n\nBM = BN = sin20\u00b0\n\nMN = 2 sin10\u00b0 sin20\u00b0\n\nNow, to find the angles of triangle BM